  "archive_id": "BW2-B79-P02",
  "title": "Finite Corners Do Not Determine Closed Cones of Normal Completely Positive Maps Without Cut–Pad Stability",
  "batch_label": "79",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "disproved",
  "scope": "For every infinite-dimensional complex Hilbert space H, there is a point-ultraweakly closed proper convex cone K contained in the normal completely positive maps B(H) -> B(H) such that K_{Q,P} = CP_{Q,P} for every pair of finite-rank orthogonal projections P,Q. Explicitly, for a unit e, E = |e><e|, and A = 2E-I, the cone K = {Phi in CP^sigma : <e,Phi(A)e> <= 0} has these properties and is not cut--pad stable.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
